"<p>Nitrobase runs as a single-instance control plane (one app container + one PostgreSQL 16 container) that manages one or more Linux servers over SSH or local host execution—without installing resident agents or Kubernetes on your servers.</p>\n<h2>High-Level Topology</h2>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-mermaid\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">flowchart</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> LR</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">  you</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">([</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">You / AI Agent</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">])</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> -->|</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">HTTPS / REST / MCP</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">|</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\"> panel</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">[</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Nitrobase Panel&#x3C;br/>TanStack Start + Bun + Postgres 16\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">  panel </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">-->|</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">SSH2 / Local nsenter</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">|</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\"> s1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">[</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Server A&#x3C;br/>Docker + Traefik v3\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">  panel </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">-->|</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">SSH2 / Local nsenter</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">|</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\"> s2</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">[</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Server B&#x3C;br/>Docker + Traefik v3\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">  s1 </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">--></span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\"> a1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">[</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Supabase / Appwrite / PocketBase\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">  s2 </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">--></span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\"> a2</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">[</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Standalone DBs / Git Apps / Custom Compose\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">  panel </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">-->|</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">rclone Backups</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">|</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\"> dest</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">[(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"S3 / R2 / B2 / Local\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">)]</span></span></code></pre>\n<h2>Control Plane</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Single-instance design:</strong> Run <strong>one</strong> Nitrobase panel instance per database. Job queues, per-server and per-app locks, cron schedulers (backups, monitoring, update checks, scheduled tasks), and SSE/WebSocket streams live in-process for predictable memory usage (~300 MB RAM) and zero external broker overhead.</li>\n<li><strong>Database:</strong> Bundled <code>postgres:16-alpine</code> (never published to the host network) accessed via Drizzle ORM.</li>\n<li><strong>Secrets at rest:</strong> All sensitive values (SSH keys, app env vars, database passwords, backup destination credentials, notification secrets) are encrypted with <code>ENCRYPTION_KEY</code> using AES-256-GCM + HKDF-SHA256 (Format v3).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Managed Server Layout</h2>\n<p>Every managed server runs standard Docker Engine and a <strong>Traefik v3</strong> reverse proxy (<code>nitrobase-traefik</code>). Nitrobase stores all managed state under <code>NITROBASE_ROOT</code> (default <code>/etc/nitrobase</code>):</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-text\"><span class=\"line\"><span>/etc/nitrobase/</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  apps/&#x3C;folder>/                  # Rendered docker-compose.yml, .env (0600), service-env/, app data</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  traefik/</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    traefik.yml                   # Static Traefik v3 config</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    dynamic/</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>      middlewares.yml             # Shared security headers &#x26; middlewares</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>      app-&#x3C;key>.yml               # Flat per-app routing files</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    acme/acme.json                # Let's Encrypt certificates</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  tunnel/cloudflared.env          # Cloudflare Tunnel token (0600), when enabled</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  backup-work/                    # Ephemeral staging area (swept after jobs)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  git-inspect/                    # Ephemeral shallow clones during Git wizard inspection</span></span></code></pre>\n<h2>Network Isolation</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Per-app private network:</strong> Each app's compose services communicate on their own private Docker default network.</li>\n<li><strong>Shared proxy network (<code>nitrobase-network</code>):</strong> Compose files are never allowed to declare <code>nitrobase-network</code> directly. Instead, Nitrobase attaches only routed containers (<code>nitrobase.routed=true</code>) after <code>up</code>/<code>start</code> by <strong>container name only</strong> (no service-name alias), preventing two apps with a <code>kong</code> or <code>web</code> service from colliding.</li>\n<li><strong>Per-link database networks (<code>nitrobase-link-&#x3C;id></code>):</strong> Linking an app to a standalone database attaches only the linked containers to a dedicated bridge network.</li>\n<li><strong>Isolated tunnel network (<code>nitrobase-tunnel</code>):</strong> When Cloudflare Tunnel is enabled, Traefik binds its private tunnel entrypoint (<code>:8081</code>) on a dedicated subnet (<code>172.31.254.0/29</code>) reachable only by <code>nitrobase-cloudflared</code>, never by app containers or the public internet.</li>\n<li><strong>Panel network (<code>nitrobase-panel</code>):</strong> When serving the panel itself through Traefik, Traefik reaches <code>nitrobase_app:3000</code> over a dedicated private network.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Jobs &#x26; Locks</h2>\n<p>Deployments, backups, restores, updates, moves, and server bootstraps run as tracked <strong>Jobs</strong> with live log streaming (SSE), per-server and per-app locking, and clean startup recovery if the panel restarts mid-job.</p>"